  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "Prove that\n$$\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta=\\frac34+\\frac14\\cos4\\theta.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta=\\frac34+\\frac14\\cos4\\theta$.\n\nExpand $(\\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta)^2$, then use the double-angle and reduction formulas.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\sin^{4}\\theta+2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta-2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos^{2}\\theta\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=(\\sin^{2}\\theta+\\cos^{2}\\theta)^2-2\\sin^{2}\\theta\\cos^{2}\\theta\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=1-2(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)^2\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=1-2\\left(\\frac12\\sin2\\theta\\right)^2\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=1-\\frac12\\sin^{2}2\\theta\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=1-\\frac12\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos4\\theta}{2}\\right)\\\\\n\\sin^{4}\\theta+\\cos^{4}\\theta&=\\frac34+\\frac14\\cos4\\theta.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 66
  },
